<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thomas Butler, 10th Earl of Ormond</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1531–<a href="/years/1614">1614</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Black Tom</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Thomas Butler, 10th Earl of Ormond, known as Black Tom, was a powerful Irish nobleman raised at the English court and a cousin and favourite of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-i">Elizabeth I</a>. He fought his rivals the FitzGeralds of Desmond and commanded the forces that crushed the second Desmond Rebellion. He built the Elizabethan manor house at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carrick-on-suir">Carrick-on-Suir</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thomas-butler-10th-earl-of-ormond.jpg" alt="Thomas Butler, 10th Earl of Ormond" width="320" height="442" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Steven van der Meulen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Steven_van_der_Meulen_Thomas_Butler_Earl_of_Ormonde_NGI.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
